[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"genie_lamp_001\",\n    \"category\": \"meaning\",\n    \"question\": \"What is the nature of life as both gift and wish, and how does our will shape existence?\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Life is a Magical Genie Lamp that you venture across, and think to wish that a magical lamp is there. As a form of Perfection, whatever we call God, or a pair of higher identities, Life is a culmination of Virtue. It is a gift, given into open hands. It is exactly as you want, as you are the reason for it to be. It is a wish, you think to have. The perfect one. Being alive, Forever.\",\n    \"themes\": [\"gift\", \"wish\", \"will\", \"perfection\", \"virtue\", \"divinity\", \"creation\", \"eternity\"],\n    \"image_prompts\": [\n      \"A magical genie lamp glowing with infinite light, emerging from a traveler's journey\",\n      \"Open hands receiving both gift and wish simultaneously\",\n      \"Life itself as a perfect, crystalline lamp radiating divine virtue\",\n      \"A figure realizing the lamp they seek was within them all along\",\n      \"Eternal life manifesting as light that never dims\"\n    ],\n    \"metadata\": {\n      \"difficulty\": \"advanced\",\n      \"philosophical_school\": \"metaphysics, theism, existentialism\",\n      \"keywords\": [\"life\", \"gift\", \"wish\", \"will\", \"perfection\", \"virtue\", \"divinity\", \"creation\", \"eternity\", \"genie lamp\"],\n      \"created_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n      \"contributor\": \"TrainPassenger\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"god_creator_001\",\n    \"category\": \"existential\",\n    \"question\": \"What is the responsibility of creation, and how do we balance perfection with compassion for the struggle?\",\n    \"perspective\": \"I'm a God, standing at a table. Creating Life with my will. Obviously, you want the best, but there is a voice, saying what about the rest, also. The Heros, the fight, to the death, for the cause you stand for. For, Redemption, Salvation, Absolution. A moment in time, outside Perfection, for the wild to be tamed and loved too.\",\n    \"themes\": [\"creation\", \"divinity\", \"responsibility\", \"heroism\", \"struggle\", \"redemption\", \"compassion\", \"sacrifice\"],\n    \"image_prompts\": [\n      \"A deity at a cosmic table, contemplating the balance between perfection and struggle\",\n      \"Heroes rising from darkness, fighting for redemption and salvation\",\n      \"A moment suspended between perfection and the wild, untamed world\",\n      \"Light and shadow in conversation, neither dismissing the other\",\n      \"The price of creation: beauty born from struggle and sacrifice\"\n    ],\n    \"metadata\": {\n      \"difficulty\": \"advanced\",\n      \"philosophical_school\": \"theology, ethics, existentialism\",\n      \"keywords\": [\"creation\", \"god\", \"responsibility\", \"heroism\", \"struggle\", \"redemption\", \"salvation\", \"compassion\", \"divine will\"],\n      \"created_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n      \"contributor\": \"TrainPassenger\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"interesting_place_001\",\n    \"category\": \"existential\",\n    \"question\": \"In a world of heroes, dragons, light, and shadow, what is our role and understanding?\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Here we are, in an interesting place. Here, we find Superman. We hear The Dragon roar. We get lost along the rode, and the shadows, have masters. Here we see a Light, and our ungraceful fall, and the Light, running into the darkness, dancing in the corner. Here we start to say, we've seen it all.\",\n    \"themes\": [\"heroism\", \"darkness\", \"light\", \"journey\", \"loss\", \"wonder\", \"transcendence\", \"knowledge\"],\n    \"image_prompts\": [\n      \"Superman and Dragon in eternal confrontation, neither winning completely\",\n      \"A road that gets lost, shadows with their own sovereignty and masters\",\n      \"Light dancing with darkness in shadowed corners, both alive\",\n      \"An ungraceful fall caught in divine light\",\n      \"A figure who thought they'd seen it all, humbled by mystery\"\n    ],\n    \"metadata\": {\n      \"difficulty\": \"advanced\",\n      \"philosophical_school\": \"existentialism, cosmology, mythology\",\n      \"keywords\": [\"heroism\", \"light\", \"darkness\", \"journey\", \"wonder\", \"transcendence\", \"shadow\", \"knowledge\"],\n      \"created_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n      \"contributor\": \"TrainPassenger\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"dharma_cycle_001\",\n    \"category\": \"meaning\",\n    \"question\": \"How does the universal order relate to human psychology, death, and the cycle of attachment and loss?\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Dharma - The Universe is in fact orderly. Hinduism ties together, our psychology. Death, an action, to a circumstance. We are so diligent, we seek destruction, to have all of what we value. Love lost, and placing flowers on graves.\",\n    \"themes\": [\"dharma\", \"order\", \"death\", \"psychology\", \"attachment\", \"loss\", \"ritual\", \"impermanence\"],\n    \"image_prompts\": [\n      \"The cosmic order flowing through human hearts and minds\",\n      \"Flowers placed on graves, beauty honoring mortality\",\n      \"The cycle of attachment and loss, eternally turning\",\n      \"Death as sacred action within universal order\",\n      \"Hands reaching toward what they value, knowing they will let it go\"\n    ],\n    \"metadata\": {\n      \"difficulty\": \"advanced\",\n      \"philosophical_school\": \"dharma, Hinduism, Buddhism, philosophy of death\",\n      \"keywords\": [\"dharma\", \"order\", \"death\", \"attachment\", \"impermanence\", \"psychology\", \"ritual\", \"loss\"],\n      \"created_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n      \"contributor\": \"TrainPassenger\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"veil_reaper_001\",\n    \"category\": \"consciousness\",\n    \"question\": \"What lies beyond the veil of illusion, and how do mortality and redemption dance together?\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Pull back the Veil. The reaper, and his black, dark toned, cloth. The coin, The wager of Sin. The Cup, for The Party. The Skeleton, the world, vain, after the greedy and selfish. A Lantern, that goes out. (Rekindled by a mysterious stranger.)\",\n    \"themes\": [\"death\", \"illusion\", \"redemption\", \"vanity\", \"greed\", \"mystery\", \"transcendence\", \"hope\"],\n    \"image_prompts\": [\n      \"The veil between worlds, held by graceful hands\",\n      \"Death as guide, not enemy, wrapped in midnight cloth\",\n      \"A coin spinning between sin and redemption\",\n      \"A cup of celebration held by skeletal hands\",\n      \"A lantern extinguished, then mysteriously rekindled by an unseen hand\",\n      \"The reaper dancing with a mysterious stranger in candlelight\"\n    ],\n    \"metadata\": {\n      \"difficulty\": \"advanced\",\n      \"philosophical_school\": \"metaphysics, tarot, mysticism, mortality studies\",\n      \"keywords\": [\"death\", \"reaper\", \"illusion\", \"veil\", \"redemption\", \"sin\", \"vanity\", \"mystery\", \"hope\", \"mortality\"],\n      \"created_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n      \"contributor\": \"TrainPassenger\"\n    }\n  }\n]\n"